                "ImageDescription": {
                  "value": "Mitosis is the process of the division of general cells. It goes through the process once, and produces two haploid daughter cells after sister chromatids line up and separate. Meiosis, on the other hand, is the process of the division of zygotes. It goes through the process of cell division twice, and the first time, homologous chromosomes line up instead of sister chromatids. When they line up, they cross some of their parts over to induce genetic variation.",
